Build fixes for cross-compiling Mesa's vc4 driver for ARMv6 (Raspberry Pi 1 /
Zero), which is what QEMU's raspi1ap machine is.

Mesa adds -mfpu=neon for any host_machine.cpu_family() == 'arm', with no ARMv7
check.  That is fine on Debian armhf, whose baseline is ARMv7 with NEON, but the
armel/ARMv6 target this build uses has neither -- and its soft-float ABI makes
gcc emit '.fpu softvfp', so the NEON intrinsics assemble to instructions the
assembler then rejects.

Give just those two objects an ARMv7 target and the softfp ABI (same calling
convention as soft, but FPU instructions allowed).  Both are optimizations
guarded at runtime by util_get_cpu_caps()->has_neon, which is false on ARM1176,
so the ARMv7 code is never reached on the target this is built for.

--- a/src/broadcom/meson.build	2023-10-04 15:53:02
+++ b/src/broadcom/meson.build	2026-08-17 02:02:43
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 
 v3d_neon_c_args = []
 if host_machine.cpu_family() == 'arm'
-    v3d_neon_c_args = '-mfpu=neon'
+    v3d_neon_c_args = ['-march=armv7-a', '-mfpu=neon', '-mfloat-abi=softfp']
 endif
 
 libv3d_neon = static_library(
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/vc4/meson.build	2023-10-04 15:53:02
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/vc4/meson.build	2026-08-17 02:09:53
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@
     include_directories : [
       inc_src, inc_include, inc_gallium, inc_gallium_aux, inc_broadcom
     ],
-    c_args : '-mfpu=neon',
+    c_args : ['-march=armv7-a', '-mfpu=neon', '-mfloat-abi=softfp'],
   )
   vc4_c_args += '-DUSE_ARM_ASM'
 endif
